      "writtenOn": "2026-08-02T16:40:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "./build-qemu-image.sh $VERSION_QEMU_IMAGE $VERSION_QEMU_IMAGE\n\nThis reuses one variable for two semantically distinct parameters (guest OS version vs. host container tag) — a DRY violation that isn\u0027t actually DRY, since it tightly couples two independently-varying values instead of eliminating real duplication. It directly contradicts the use case you described.\n\n\nSuggestion:\n\nbash\n./build-qemu-image.sh $VERSION_QEMU_IMAGE $VERSION_COMPILE_QEMU\n\nThat\u0027s also the answer to my original comment — not a missing VERSION_COMPILE_GTESTS, but a variable used outside its intended scope.\n\nAlso, once thread 1\u0027s fix lands (stripping moved into load_config.sh), there\u0027s no need for VERSION_QEMU_IMAGE, VERSION_COMPILE_KERNEL, VERSION_COMPILE_QEMU, VERSION_COMPILE_HTESTS as separate locals at all — that\u0027s an unnecessary indirection layer. Just reference EVSSIM_GUEST_TESTS_GUEST_VM_IMAGE, EVSSIM_KERNEL_COMPILE_CONTAINER, etc. directly at each call site. Simpler code, one less place for the two values to accidentally drift apart, and no naming to keep in sync with the config loader.",
      "parentUuid": "2cdae6aa_05606d35",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "9527c8354a905c46ec347d5dbfb33fbcb842012e",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
